  "goodToKnow": "Die Geologie is geology, the study of the earth's structure and rocks. Der Geologe (weak noun) is a geologist, and geologisch geological. German geologists played a key role in the field: Alfred Wegener proposed continental drift in 1912. The Geopark network in Germany showcases landscapes like the volcanic Eifel, with its maars. Geography is die Geografie or, in school, Erdkunde. It has no plural."
